# File: PRICING_NOTE.md

# Pricing Note: Value of Automation

## Manual Process (Current)

The operations team currently runs the Monday report manually every week.

- Time: 30-45 minutes per week to open DB tool, type SQL, export and clean in Excel
- Cost: ~2-3 hours/month of staff time
- Risk: Typos in county name, date range, or formula lead to incorrect revenue numbers
- Dependency: Only 1-2 people know the queries
- Limitation: Requires database tool installed, cannot run on any machine

## Automated Solution (This Script)

- Time: <10 seconds - `get_county_report(county, start_date, end_date)`
- Output: Clean, consistent summary table: `product, total_orders, total_quantity, total_revenue_kes`
- Safety: Parameterized queries (no SQL injection), handles no-results gracefully
- Portability: Runs on any machine with Python + Supabase credentials
- Scalable: Ready to plug into dashboard, WhatsApp bot, or automated email

## Business Value

1.  Time Saved: 2-3 hours/month freed for operations
2.  Accuracy: Eliminates manual errors in weekly management reports
3.  Continuity: Any team member can generate the report, not just DB admin
4.  Speed: Monday report ready before 8 AM without manual work

## Suggested Pricing

Charge for the outcome, not the code.

-One-time Automation: 5,000 - 15,000 KES
  Includes script + setup + README + 1 training call

-Monthly Service (if you host & auto-send): 2,500 - 5,000 KES / month
  Includes hosting, auto Monday email, and support for new counties

If staff cost is ~600 KES/hour, manual reporting costs the client 1,500 - 2,400 KES/month in wasted time alone. 
Automation pays for itself in month 1.
